<div id="unified-endpoint-management" v-cloak>
  <div purpose="page-container">
    <div purpose="page-content">
      <div purpose="hero-and-top-section">
        <div purpose="page-hero">
          <div purpose="page-hero-content">
            <div purpose="page-hero-headings">
              <h4>Unified endpoint management</h4>
              <h1>Every Mac, PC, Linux laptop, and phone in one console</h1>
            </div>
            <div purpose="page-hero-text">
              <p>Most IT teams run one tool for Macs, another for Windows, and a spreadsheet for Linux. Fleet manages macOS, Windows, Linux, iOS, iPadOS, Android, and ChromeOS with one inventory, one set of policies, and live answers from every device. NVIDIA, Stripe, and Epic Games already run Fleet.</p>
            </div>
            <div purpose="button-row" class="d-flex">
              <a purpose="cta-button" class="btn btn-primary" href="#demo">Get a demo</a>
              <animated-arrow-button href="#checklist">What to ask every UEM vendor</animated-arrow-button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="page-hero-image">
            <img alt="Filtering devices by platform in Fleet: macOS, Windows, Linux, ChromeOS, iOS, iPadOS, and Android" src="/images/windows-filter-by-platform-600x450@2x.png">
          </div>
        </div>
        <div purpose="top-section">
          <div purpose="page-section">
            <div purpose="feature-text">
              <h2>One license for all of your operating systems</h2>
              <p>Enroll, configure, patch, and secure every device from the same place, whatever it runs.</p>
              <div purpose="capability-list">
                <div purpose="capability"><img alt="" aria-hidden="true" src="/images/icon-checkmark-green-16x16@2x.png"><span>macOS</span></div>
                <div purpose="capability"><img alt="" aria-hidden="true" src="/images/icon-checkmark-green-16x16@2x.png"><span>Windows</span></div>
                <div purpose="capability"><img alt="" aria-hidden="true" src="/images/icon-checkmark-green-16x16@2x.png"><span>Linux</span></div>
                <div purpose="capability"><img alt="" aria-hidden="true" src="/images/icon-checkmark-green-16x16@2x.png"><span>iOS and iPadOS</span></div>
                <div purpose="capability"><img alt="" aria-hidden="true" src="/images/icon-checkmark-green-16x16@2x.png"><span>Android</span></div>
                <div purpose="capability"><img alt="" aria-hidden="true" src="/images/icon-checkmark-green-16x16@2x.png"><span>ChromeOS</span></div>
                <div purpose="capability"><img alt="" aria-hidden="true" src="/images/icon-checkmark-green-16x16@2x.png"><span>FileVault, BitLocker, and LUKS2</span></div>
                <div purpose="capability"><img alt="" aria-hidden="true" src="/images/icon-checkmark-green-16x16@2x.png"><span>OS update deadlines</span></div>
                <div purpose="capability"><img alt="" aria-hidden="true" src="/images/icon-checkmark-green-16x16@2x.png"><span>Lock and wipe, Linux included</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div purpose="page-section">
            <div purpose="banner">
              <div purpose="banner-text">
                <div purpose="banner-heading">
                  <h2>Why teams go shopping for a UEM</h2>
                </div>
                <div purpose="banner-body">
                  <div purpose="banner-item">
                    <h5>A console for every OS</h5>
                    <p>Macs live in one tool and PCs in another. A change that should go to every device turns into the same job done two or three times.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div purpose="banner-item">
                    <h5>Security works from exports</h5>
                    <p>When a new vulnerability lands, someone runs a report in each tool and stitches the results together before anyone knows how exposed you are.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div purpose="banner-item">
                    <h5>Audits mean a week of screenshots</h5>
                    <p>Proving every device is encrypted and patched means pulling evidence from every tool and hoping nothing slipped between them.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div purpose="banner-image"></div>
            </div>
            <div purpose="callout">
              <div purpose="callout-text">
                <h3>See your whole device mix in one place</h3>
                <p>Tell us what you run today, and see that same mix managed from one console.</p>
              </div>
              <a purpose="cta-button" class="btn btn-primary" href="#demo">Get a demo</a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div purpose="page-section">
            <div purpose="section-heading">
              <div purpose="kicker-text">
                <img alt="Introducing Fleet" src="/images/endpoint-governance-introducing-fleet-193x28@2x.png">
              </div>
              <h2>Device management and device security, in the same tool</h2>
            </div>
            <div purpose="three-column-list" class="sm-gap">
              <div purpose="feature">
                <div purpose="feature-title">
                  <h5>One set of policies</h5>
                </div>
                <p>Write a control once and enforce it on every OS. Check devices against CIS benchmarks, SOC 2, ISO, or your own baseline and see results in seconds.</p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="feature">
                <div purpose="feature-title">
                  <h5>Patching that runs itself</h5>
                </div>
                <p>Install from a catalog of Fleet-maintained apps or your own packages. When a device falls out of compliance, Fleet installs the fix. No ticket needed.</p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="feature">
                <div purpose="feature-title">
                  <h5>Answers in seconds</h5>
                </div>
                <p>Fleet keeps a live connection to every device, so you can ask any question about your fleet and get an answer from the devices themselves.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div purpose="button-row">
              <a purpose="cta-button" class="btn btn-primary" href="#demo">Get a demo</a>
              <animated-arrow-button href="#checklist">What to ask every UEM vendor</animated-arrow-button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="features-section">
        <div purpose="feature-with-image-row">
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="Device details in Fleet, reported live" src="/images/mdm-visibility-800x450@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="image-caption">
              <h5>Every device in one inventory</h5>
              <p>Apple, Windows, Linux, and personal devices show up in the same list, with the same details, reported live.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="Vulnerabilities found on installed software" src="/images/homepage-vulnerability-management-table-617x440@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="image-caption">
              <h5>Vulnerabilities found where they live</h5>
              <p>Installed software on every OS is checked against known vulnerabilities, so security and IT work from the same list.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="quote-and-logos">
        <div purpose="section-quote">
          <div purpose="quote-author-image">
            <img alt="Mason Peressini" src="/images/testimonial-author-mason-peressini-100x100@2x.png">
          </div>
          <div purpose="quote-content">
          <p purpose="quote-text">“I’m saving 20 hours per week managing devices.”</p>
          <div purpose="quote-author-info">
            <div purpose="name-and-title">
              <p purpose="author-name">Mason Peressini</p>
              <p purpose="author-title">Sr Systems Support Specialist, Reed College</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div purpose="logo-grid" class="d-none d-sm-flex">
          <div purpose="logo-row">
            <div purpose="logo" class="nvidia">
              <img alt="NVIDIA logo" src="/images/logos/logo-nvidia-color-161x32@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="logo" class="stripe">
              <img alt="Stripe logo" src="/images/stripe-logo-96x40@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="logo" class="epic">
              <img alt="Epic Games logo" src="/images/logos/logo-epic-games-40x46@2x.png">
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="logo-row">
            <div purpose="logo" class="thumbtack">
              <img alt="Thumbtack logo" src="/images/thumbtack-logo-197x40@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="logo" class="fastly">
              <img alt="Fastly logo" src="/images/logos/logo-fastly-color-70x28@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="logo" class="faire">
              <img alt="Faire logo" src="/images/faire-logo-192x40@2x.png">
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div purpose="logo-grid" class="d-flex d-sm-none">
          <div purpose="logo-row">
            <div purpose="logo" class="nvidia">
              <img alt="NVIDIA logo" src="/images/logos/logo-nvidia-color-161x32@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="logo" class="stripe">
              <img alt="Stripe logo" src="/images/stripe-logo-96x40@2x.png">
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="logo-row">
            <div purpose="logo" class="epic">
              <img alt="Epic Games logo" src="/images/logos/logo-epic-games-40x46@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="logo" class="thumbtack">
              <img alt="Thumbtack logo" src="/images/thumbtack-logo-197x40@2x.png">
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="logo-row">
            <div purpose="logo" class="fastly">
              <img alt="Fastly logo" src="/images/logos/logo-fastly-color-70x28@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="logo" class="faire">
              <img alt="Faire logo" src="/images/faire-logo-192x40@2x.png">
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="page-section" id="checklist">
        <div purpose="comparison">
          <div purpose="comparison-intro">
            <h2>What to ask every UEM vendor</h2>
            <p>Most UEM tools cover the basics on Mac, Windows, and phones. The differences show up in the questions below. Ask each vendor you’re looking at, and here is how Fleet answers.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="comparison-grid">
            <div purpose="comparison-head">
              <span>The question</span>
              <span>Fleet’s answer</span>
            </div>
            <% [
              { question: 'Is Linux managed like everything else?',
                answer: 'Yes. Linux gets the same inventory, policies, scripts, disk encryption, and lock and wipe as macOS and Windows.' },
              { question: 'How old is the device data you’re looking at?',
                answer: 'Seconds. Fleet keeps a live connection to every device and answers from the device itself.' },
              { question: 'Is vulnerability detection included, or sold separately?',
                answer: 'Included, on every OS, with no add-on to buy.' },
              { question: 'Can devices fix themselves when they fall out of compliance?',
                answer: 'Yes. A failing policy can install software or run a script automatically, without a ticket.' },
              { question: 'Can changes be reviewed and rolled back?',
                answer: 'Yes. Keep profiles, policies, and software as code, review changes before they ship, and roll back if something goes wrong.' },
              { question: 'Can it run on our own infrastructure?',
                answer: 'Yes. Fleet can host it for you, or you can run it on-prem, in your cloud, or air-gapped with the same features.' },
              { question: 'Do we have to wipe devices to switch?',
                answer: 'No. Windows moves with automatic MDM migration. Macs, iPhones, and iPads on version 26 in Apple Business Manager can use Apple’s native MDM migration.' },
            ].forEach((row)=>{ %>
            <div purpose="comparison-row">
              <div purpose="comparison-capability"><%= row.question %></div>
              <div purpose="comparison-cell" class="yes">
                <span purpose="comparison-label">Fleet</span>
                <span purpose="comparison-value"><%= row.answer %></span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <% }); %>
          </div>
          <div purpose="callout">
            <div purpose="callout-text">
              <h3>Ask us these questions too</h3>
              <p>Bring your device counts and the tools you use today, and we’ll answer for your setup.</p>
            </div>
            <a purpose="cta-button" class="btn btn-primary" href="#demo">Get a demo</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="features-section">
        <div purpose="feature-with-image-row">
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="Compliance policies passing across devices" src="/images/feature-image-prove-compliance-800x600@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="image-caption">
              <h5>Audit evidence on demand</h5>
              <p>Run live checks against your baselines and answer auditor questions on the spot, instead of gathering screenshots for weeks.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="Automations that install software when a policy fails" src="/images/feature-image-stop-chasing-patches-800x600@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="image-caption">
              <h5>Fixes that run on their own</h5>
              <p>When a device fails a policy, Fleet can install the update or run a script to fix it, on any OS.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-with-image-row">
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="A GitOps workflow for device configuration" src="/images/fleet-gitops-workflow-471x337@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="image-caption">
              <h5>Changes your whole team can see</h5>
              <p>Make changes in Fleet’s UI, from Slack or Microsoft Teams, or as code. Every change has an audit history, whoever made it.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="Running a live report across devices" src="/images/run-query-800x537@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="image-caption">
              <h5>Ask any question, on every OS</h5>
              <p>Write a report once and run it across Macs, PCs, and Linux. Results come back from the devices themselves.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="page-section" id="migration">
        <div purpose="section-with-image">
          <div purpose="feature-text">
            <h3>Switching doesn’t mean starting over</h3>
            <p>You don’t have to move everything on day one. Run Fleet alongside the tool you have today and see every device without disrupting anyone. Then move one group at a time. Windows devices move with automatic MDM migration, without a wipe and without the user doing anything. Macs, iPhones, and iPads on version 26 in Apple Business Manager can use Apple’s native MDM migration. Linux devices join by installing Fleet’s agent.</p>
            <div purpose="section-buttons">
              <a purpose="cta-button" class="btn btn-primary" href="#demo">Get a demo</a>
              <animated-arrow-button href="#checklist">What to ask every UEM vendor</animated-arrow-button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="section-image">
            <img alt="A device's details in Fleet after migration" src="/images/mdm-feature-image-1-344x288@2x.png">
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div purpose="tweets-container" class="container-fluid px-md-0 pb-0 d-flex flex-column justify-content-center">
